Today I am very happy.
Now I have a new phone number.
I am thirty-one years old.
But today I am happy like a little girl.
I stop near a stall on the street.
There is a lot of crowd there.
I say to the shopkeeper, "Dada, I want one vada pav."
"And I want one cutting chai too."
Dada says, "Yes, madam."
He gives me a hot vada pav.
I eat the vada pav.
It is very spicy.
But it is awesome!
Then I drink the cutting chai.
I ask, "Dada, how many rupees?"
Dada says, "Twenty-five rupees, madam."
I give him twenty-five rupees.
Now my life in Mumbai truly begins.
